from pathlib import Path

content = r"""# ProjeX v2 — Detailed Implementation Task List

## Development Rules

- Complete tasks in dependency order.
- Every major refactor uses one dedicated branch.
- Split large work into small commits that can be reviewed and reverted independently.
- Every feature must include validation, authorization, tests, documentation, and UI states where applicable.
- Merge only after CI passes and the feature has been manually verified.
- Use feature branches from the relevant refactor or development branch; avoid creating a branch for every small task.

## Branching Strategy

| Branch | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `main` | Stable production-ready code |
| `develop` | Integration branch for completed features |
| `refactor/ui-foundation` | UI audit, design system, layout, and reusable components |
| `refactor/backend-nestjs` | Express-to-NestJS migration and backend restructuring |
| `feature/<phase>-<feature>` | Independent feature work |
| `hotfix/<issue>` | Urgent production fixes |

### Branch Rules

- Use `refactor/ui-foundation` for the complete UI foundation migration.
- Use `refactor/backend-nestjs` for the complete NestJS migration.
- Create feature branches only for independently testable business features.
- Do not create separate branches for every small component, endpoint, or test.
- Merge refactor branches into `develop` only after regression testing.
- Keep frontend and backend refactors separate, but coordinate through API contracts.

---

# Phase 0 — Architecture, Testing & Development Foundation

## 0.1 Codebase Audit

- [x] Inventory frontend routes, layouts, components, hooks, state, and API calls.
  - [x] Identify duplicated components and utilities.
  - [x] Identify static, mock, and hardcoded data.
  - [x] Identify unused files and dependencies.
  - [x] Record existing UI and API issues.
